  "worked_solution": "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}v-u{v}^{\u2032}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=-{h}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{\u2032}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}v-u{v}^{\u2032}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-{h}^{\u2032}(t))\\cdot z(t)-(1-h(t))\\cdot {z}^{\u2032}(t)}{(z(t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-z(t){h}^{\u2032}(t)-{z}^{\u2032}(t)(1-h(t))}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=2,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(2) & =\\frac{-z(2){h}^{\u2032}(2)-{z}^{\u2032}(2)(1-h(2))}{{z}^{2}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (1-5)}{{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24+16}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
